## OAuth

### `oauth_client`
`PERMISSIONS NONE` (no client-side access — server-only).
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | string | `ASSERT $value != NONE`, unique index — also the OAuth `client_id` |
| `secret_hash` | option\<string\> | bcrypt hash; absent for public/PKCE-only clients |
| `redirect_uris` | array\<string\> | DEFAULT [] |
| `scopes` | array\<string\> | DEFAULT [] — scopes this client may request |
| `auto_grant_scopes` | bool | DEFAULT false — skip consent screen |
| `public` | bool | DEFAULT false — PKCE-only, no secret |
| `db_name` | option\<string\> | added in migration 013 (currently unused — see [project_oauth_client_gql](/docs/api) history; per-client DBs now live in `client_database`) |

### `grant`
A user's consent for a client to use a set of scopes.
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `user` | record\<user\> | |
| `client` | record\<oauth_client\> | |
| `scopes` | array\<string\> | granted scopes |
| `enabled` | bool | DEFAULT true |
| `created_at` | datetime | DEFAULT `time::now()`, READONLY |
| `updated_at` | datetime | DEFAULT `time::now()` |

Unique index on `(user, client)` — one grant record per user/client pair;
scopes are merged/updated in place as consent is extended.

### `refresh_token`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `user` | record\<user\> | |
| `client` | record\<oauth_client\> | |
| `scopes` | array\<string\> | scopes granted at issuance |
| `expires_at` | datetime | |
| `created_at` | datetime | DEFAULT `time::now()`, READONLY |
| `revoked` | bool | DEFAULT false |
| `used` | bool | DEFAULT false — rotation-lock flag; reuse after `used=true` revokes the grant |

Indexes on `user`, `client`, `expires_at`.

---

## Versioning pattern

`contact`/`media` follow the shared versioning pattern documented in the
project's `CLAUDE.md`:

- **`<entity>`** holds current state, plus `version -> <entity>_version`
  (pointer to the latest version) and standard `created_at`
  (`VALUE $before OR time::now() READONLY`, allows backfilled timestamps)
  / `updated_at` (`VALUE time::now()`).
- **`<entity>_version`** is append-only: every field `READONLY`, mirrors
  the entity's data plus `<entity>_id` back-reference and its own
  `created_at`.
- **`derived_from`** — a single `TYPE RELATION` table (no IN/OUT type
  constraint) shared by *all* versioned entities, connecting
  `old_version -> derived_from -> new_version`. Enables full ancestry graph
  traversal, including merges (multiple parents).

Writes follow the transactional create/update pattern in `CLAUDE.md`
(`BEGIN TRANSACTION ... COMMIT TRANSACTION`), with the caller supplying
`parentVersionIds` for updates so non-linear history (merges) is supported.

### `contact` / `contact_version`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `user` | record\<user\> | READONLY (owner) |
| `name` | string | |
| `email` | string | |
| `phone` | option\<string\> | |
| `created_at` | datetime | VALUE `$before OR time::now()`, READONLY |
| `updated_at` | datetime | VALUE `time::now()` |
| `version` | record\<contact_version\> | pointer to latest version |

`contact_version` mirrors `name`/`email`/`phone` (all READONLY) plus
`contact_id -> record<contact>` and its own `created_at`.

### `media` / `media_version`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `user` | record\<user\> | READONLY (owner) |
| `filename` | string | |
| `mime_type` | string | |
| `size` | int | sum of chunk sizes |
| `chunks` | array\<record\<chunk\>\> | ordered chunk references |
| `created_at` | datetime | VALUE `$before OR time::now()`, READONLY |
| `updated_at` | datetime | VALUE `time::now()` |
| `version` | record\<media_version\> | pointer to latest version |

`media_version` mirrors `filename`/`mime_type`/`size`/`chunks` (all
READONLY) plus `media_id -> record<media>` and its own `created_at`.

